        "chapter_1_year": "2011",
        "chapter_1_heading": "The Meeting",
        "chapter_1_body": "Zach and Harin met in pharmacy school in 2011. What began as a friendship grew into years spent working in pharmacy, learning to think carefully about formulation, ingredients, and the details that matter.",
        "chapter_1_image_asset": "story-chapter1-2011.jpg",
        "chapter_2_year": "",
        "chapter_2_heading": "The Idea",
        "chapter_2_body": "Years later, skincare kept finding its way into the conversation. Zach's wife was exploring products while they traveled through Japan. Harin watched his wife piece together a routine from products she found online. The question became simple: why couldn't we make something ourselves?",
        "chapter_2_image_asset": "",
        "chapter_3_year": "",
        "chapter_3_heading": "Chemistrie",
        "chapter_3_body": "Skincare felt like a natural extension of what they already understood as pharmacists: ingredients, formulation, precision, and the importance of getting the details right. They weren't trying to reinvent skincare. They simply believed they could do it better, creating skincare with the thoughtful formulation and elevated experience they wanted to give the people closest to them.",
        "chapter_3_image_asset": "pillar-designed-together.png"
      }
